it is not a valid HTML attribute. The correct way to do this is to use the onclick attribute of the <div> element. The following example shows how to do this:

<div onclick="alert('Hello World!');">Hello World!</div>

The following example shows how to use the onclick attribute of a <div> element to call a function:

function doSomething() {
  alert('Hello World!');
  document.getElementById('myDiv').onclick = doSomething;

